<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chirmiri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chirmiri is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>-mining town in the hills of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, in the area of the former princely state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, or Koriya. The coal seams around it were opened up in the 20th century and are worked by South Eastern Coalfields, and mining remains the basis of the local economy. It lies close to the neighbouring town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manendragarh">Manendragarh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chirmiri.jpg" alt="Chirmiri" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vikassahu60 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haldibadi_2008.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The coalfields around <b>Chirmiri</b> and Manendragarh were developed in the 20th century.</blockquote><a href="/state/korea-state">Korea State</a></li></ul></section>
